This keyword specifies the datastore and key where the ceph.conf content is securely stored.

The content is automatically exposed on all nodes as a temporary file at /run/opensvc/<fqn>/key/<keyname>, allowing the file to be securely referenced by the rbd command using the -c <filename> flag.

If not set, the rbd command will fall back to /etc/ceph/ceph.conf.

Value format: `from <datastore path> key <key name>` (the path supports relative notation, e.g., ./cfg/ceph).